// ============================================================
// ARCHITECTURE
// ============================================================
//
//                    #10 MASTER
//                         │
//                  #1 PERFORMANCE
//                         │
//                  #3 POWER/THERMAL
//                         │
//                    #11 MEMORY
//                         │
//                         ▼
//                ┌─────────────────┐
//                │ #12 METAL GPU   │
//                │     RUNTIME     │
//                └────────┬────────┘
//                         │
//          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
//          │              │              │
//       PIPELINES      BUFFERS        TEXTURES
//          │              │              │
//          └──────────────┼──────────────┘
//                         │
//                  COMMAND EXECUTOR
//                         │
//                  COMMAND BUFFER
//                         │
//                    MTL DEVICE
//                         │
//                       GPU
//
// ============================================================
//
// DESIGN RULES
//
// 1. Metal objects remain inside actors whenever possible.
//
// 2. Sendable descriptors cross concurrency boundaries.
//
// 3. Large resources use explicit pools.
//
// 4. Pipelines are cached.
//
// 5. GPU work is governed before submission.
//
// 6. GPU work is bounded by permits.
//
// 7. Completion is asynchronous.
//
// 8. Memory pressure trims GPU-owned pools.
//
// 9. Power policy changes GPU workload policy.
//
// 10. AI can use this runtime without owning Metal directly.
//
// 11. Rendering/UI remains a separate concern.
//
// 12. This runtime does NOT control:
//
//       - GPU frequency
//       - GPU voltage
//       - thermal firmware
//       - private driver state
//       - iOS kernel scheduling
//
