# 34. Complete Runtime Position

The iPhone stack is now:

```text
#1  Performance Runtime
        │
#3  Battery / Thermal Runtime
        │
#4  Networking Runtime
        │
#5  Persistent Storage
        │
#6  UI / Rendering
        │
#7  Security / Privacy
        │
#8  On-Device Intelligence
        │
#9  Sensor / Hardware Abstraction
        │
#10 Master Runtime
        │
#11 Advanced Memory
        │
#12 Metal / GPU
        │
#13 Advanced Camera / Imaging
        │
#14 Media / Audio
```

The most important architectural boundary introduced by **#14** is:

```text
                 APPLICATION CONCURRENCY
                         │
                Swift actors / Tasks
                         │
                         ▼
                 Audio Runtime API
                         │
                         ▼
             Dedicated Audio Queue
                         │
                         ▼
                AVAudioEngine Graph
                         │
                         ▼
              REAL-TIME AUDIO THREAD
```

That keeps the audio subsystem deterministic while the rest of the iPhone runtime remains actor-based and asynchronous.

## Public API boundary

This architecture uses Apple's public application-level audio APIs. It does **not** attempt to control:

* iOS audio-driver internals
* private Core Audio services
* hardware DSP firmware
* amplifier firmware
* codec firmware
* speaker-driver control
* CPU/GPU frequency
* private audio daemon interfaces

Those remain operating-system/hardware responsibilities.





# iPhone Database & Query Engine — Swift

## 15. Database / Query Engine

This subsystem provides an application-level persistent database runtime for the iPhone stack.

Architecture:

```text
                    MASTER RUNTIME #10
                           │
                           ▼
                 DATABASE RUNTIME #15
                           │
              ┌────────────┼────────────┐
              │            │            │
              ▼            ▼            ▼
          Connection   Transactions   Migrations
            Pool           │             │
              │            ▼             ▼
              │        Query Engine   Schema
              │            │
              └────────────┼────────────┐
                           ▼            ▼
                        SQLite       WAL
                           │
                           ▼
                    Persistent Store
```

The database layer owns structured application data.

It should not be used for:

* large media blobs
* camera frames
* unbounded PCM audio
* temporary GPU resources
* secrets that belong in Keychain/Secure Enclave

Those remain with #5, #7, #11, #12, #13 and #14 respectively.

