# 44. Final iPhone Architecture

The database now sits beneath the application's structured data flows:

```text
                         MASTER #10
                             │
        ┌────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
        │                    │                     │
        ▼                    ▼                     ▼
    POWER #3            MEMORY #11             SECURITY #7
        │                    │                     │
        └────────────────────┼─────────────────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                      DATABASE #15
                             │
          ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐
          │                  │                  │
          ▼                  ▼                  ▼
      TELEMETRY          OUTBOX             APP STATE
          │                  │                  │
          ▼                  ▼                  ▼
       Sensors          Network #4          Runtime
       Watch #9          Cloud #16          Config
       Events #7
          │
          └──────────────────┬─────────────────┐
                             │                 │
                             ▼                 ▼
                         AI #8             MEDIA
                                          #13 / #14
```

The key result of #15 is that **#5 Persistent Storage becomes a real storage architecture rather than simply a file store**:

```text
#5  Storage abstraction
        │
        ▼
#15 Database / Query Engine
        │
        ├── SQLite
        ├── WAL
        ├── transactions
        ├── migrations
        ├── indexes
        ├── repositories
        ├── retention
        └── persistent network outbox
```

This gives the iPhone runtime a durable transactional data layer while keeping high-volume media and real-time processing outside the database.





# iPhone Cloud & iCloud Runtime — Swift

## 16. Cloud / iCloud Runtime

This subsystem adds cloud persistence and synchronization to the iPhone runtime.

The architecture is:

```text
                         MASTER RUNTIME #10
                                  │
                                  ▼
                         CLOUD RUNTIME #16
                                  │
                 ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
                 │                │                │
                 ▼                ▼                ▼
             CloudKit        Sync Engine       Cloud Status
                 │                │
                 │                ▼
                 │          Conflict Resolver
                 │                │
                 ▼                ▼
              iCloud          DATABASE #15
                                │
                    ┌───────────┼────────────┐
                    ▼           ▼            ▼
                Telemetry     Outbox      App State
```

The core principle is:

```text
LOCAL DATABASE = durable application state
iCLOUD         = replicated remote state
CLOUD SYNC     = reconciliation process
```

Cloud availability must never be required for the application to function locally.

