# 38. Offline-First Architecture

The complete architecture should now behave like:

```text
                    USER ACTION
                         │
                         ▼
                    DATABASE #15
                         │
                ┌────────┴────────┐
                │                 │
                ▼                 ▼
             LOCAL             SYNC QUEUE
              STATE                 │
                │                   ▼
                │              CLOUD #16
                │                   │
                │             ┌─────┴─────┐
                │             │           │
                │          success      failure
                │             │           │
                │             ▼           ▼
                │          complete     retry
                │                         │
                └─────────────────────────┘
```

The user should not have to wait for iCloud before a local write becomes durable.

---

# 39. Conflict Flow

```text
                    LOCAL RECORD
                         │
                         ▼
                   Local Database
                         │
                         │
                  ┌──────┴──────┐
                  │             │
                  ▼             ▼
             Local version   Cloud version
                  │             │
                  └──────┬──────┘
                         ▼
                 Conflict Resolver
                         │
          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
          ▼              ▼              ▼
       local           merge          remote
        win
          │              │              │
          └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                         ▼
                  Canonical Record
                         │
                         ▼
                    Database #15
                         │
                         ▼
                     Cloud #16
```

---

# 40. Cloud + Network #4

The division of responsibility is:

```text
NETWORK #4
    │
    ├── HTTP/HTTPS
    ├── connectivity
    ├── request policy
    ├── retries
    └── network metrics

CLOUD #16
    │
    ├── CloudKit
    ├── iCloud account
    ├── cloud records
    ├── cloud assets
    ├── change tracking
    └── conflict resolution
```

CloudKit networking should not be reinvented as ordinary `URLSession` traffic.

---

# 41. Cloud + Storage #5

```text
#5 Storage
    │
    ├── files
    ├── caches
    └── local storage abstraction

#15 Database
    │
    ├── structured records
    ├── indexes
    └── durable sync queues

#16 Cloud
    │
    ├── remote records
    ├── cloud assets
    └── synchronization
```

---

# 42. Cloud + Security #7

Authentication secrets should remain in the security subsystem.

```text
#7 Security
     │
     ├── Keychain
     ├── Secure Enclave
     ├── authentication
     └── application secrets

#16 Cloud
     │
     └── CloudKit account/container state
```

Do not create a second application-specific credential vault inside the cloud runtime.

---

# 43. Cloud + AI #8

AI results can be synchronized selectively:

```text
AI inference
     │
     ▼
Local result
     │
     ├── transient → discard
     │
     ├── local-only → #15
     │
     └── user/application result
                │
                ▼
              #16
                │
                ▼
             iCloud
```

Raw inference intermediates generally do not need to be synchronized.

---

# 44. Cloud + Camera #13

Camera data should use:

```text
Image
 │
 ▼
Local file
 │
 ▼
Metadata in #15
 │
 ▼
Cloud asset queue
 │
 ▼
CloudKit asset
```

rather than:

```text
Camera frame
    ↓
Database BLOB
    ↓
Cloud record
```

---

# 45. Cloud + Audio #14

The same principle applies to audio:

```text
Audio recording
      │
      ▼
CAF / M4A / WAV
      │
      ├── local metadata → #15
      │
      └── optional cloud asset → #16
```

Real-time audio never waits for cloud synchronization.

---

# 46. Power Policy

Cloud synchronization is an ideal workload for the #3 governor.

```text
THERMAL NORMAL
    │
    └── sync normally

THERMAL ELEVATED
    │
    └── smaller batches

THERMAL HIGH
    │
    └── metadata only / defer assets

LOW POWER MODE
    │
    └── defer background synchronization

CRITICAL
    │
    └── local persistence only
```

---

# 47. Memory Policy

Cloud operations should use bounded batches.

```text
1,000,000 records
       │
       X
       │
       ▼
   NEVER LOAD ALL
       │
       ▼
   100 records
       │
       ▼
     upload
       │
       ▼
   next 100
```

This connects naturally to #11's bounded memory architecture.

---

