# 50. Production Cloud Architecture

The final intended stack is:

```text
                         iPHONE
                           │
                           ▼
                    MASTER #10
                           │
        ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐
        │                  │                  │
        ▼                  ▼                  ▼
    POWER #3           NETWORK #4         SECURITY #7
        │                  │
        │                  ▼
        │             CLOUD #16
        │                  │
        │          ┌───────┼────────┐
        │          │       │        │
        │          ▼       ▼        ▼
        │      Records   Assets   Changes
        │          │       │        │
        └──────────┼───────┼────────┘
                   ▼       ▼
                 #15 DATABASE
                   │
          ┌────────┼─────────┐
          ▼        ▼         ▼
      App State  Telemetry  Outbox
```

The resulting architecture is **offline-first, cloud-replicated and power-aware**:

```text
WRITE
  │
  ▼
LOCAL DATABASE
  │
  ├──────────────► APP CONTINUES
  │
  ▼
SYNC QUEUE
  │
  ▼
NETWORK / POWER POLICY
  │
  ├── RUN NOW
  ├── RUN LATER
  └── DEFER
  │
  ▼
CLOUDKIT
  │
  ▼
REMOTE STATE
```

The next major subsystem is **#17 — Push Notification Engine**. That layer can connect APNs, notification categories/actions, token lifecycle, silent/background notifications, CloudKit change triggers, notification scheduling, deep links, delivery diagnostics, and the #3 power/background execution policies.
::



# iPhone Push Notification Engine — Swift

## 17. Push Notification Engine

### Architecture

```text
                         MASTER RUNTIME #10
                                  │
                                  ▼
                      PUSH NOTIFICATION #17
                                  │
          ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐
          │                       │                       │
          ▼                       ▼                       ▼
     APNs Token              Notification             Deep Links
     Lifecycle                Router                   / Actions
          │                       │
          ▼                       ▼
      Remote Push          Local Event Bus #7
                                  │
             ┌────────────────────┼─────────────────┐
             ▼                    ▼                 ▼
          Cloud #16           Storage #15        UI #6
             │
             ▼
       CloudKit Changes
```

The central rule is:

```text
PUSH NOTIFICATION = EVENT / TRIGGER

DATABASE #15      = SOURCE OF TRUTH
CLOUD #16         = REMOTE REPLICATION
UI #6             = PRESENTATION
```

A notification must never be treated as authoritative application state.

