# 30. Deep-Link Flow

```text
Notification tap
      │
      ▼
UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate
      │
      ▼
PushEventRouter
      │
      ▼
NotificationDeepLinkRouter
      │
      ▼
Application Router
      │
      ▼
SwiftUI Navigation
```

The notification layer should not directly mutate application screens.

---

# 31. Security

Remote payloads should be considered untrusted input.

Validate:

```text
identifier
category
action
deep link
record identifiers
resource identifiers
command parameters
```

Never execute arbitrary commands encoded in a notification.

For sensitive operations:

```text
push
 │
 ▼
open application
 │
 ▼
authenticate #7
 │
 ▼
perform operation
```

---

# 32. Privacy

Notification content can appear on a locked device.

For sensitive information, prefer:

```text
"New activity available"
```

over embedding private application data directly into the notification.

The #7 security/redaction layer should therefore be able to classify notification payloads:

```swift
public enum NotificationPrivacyLevel:
    String,
    Sendable,
    Codable
{
    case publicContent
    case privateContent
    case sensitiveContent
}
```

---

# 33. Power Integration

Push processing should connect to #3.

```text
             PUSH ARRIVES
                  │
                  ▼
            Power Governor #3
                  │
        ┌─────────┼─────────┐
        ▼         ▼         ▼
     critical   normal   background
        │         │         │
        ▼         ▼         ▼
      execute   bounded   defer
```

A background push should perform the minimum work required to reconcile state.

---

# 34. Background Execution

The push engine should not assume unlimited background execution.

```text
APNs
 │
 ▼
iOS grants execution opportunity
 │
 ▼
small bounded task
 │
 ├── synchronize
 ├── persist
 └── schedule UI refresh
 │
 ▼
finish
```

Long-running background processing belongs in **#18 Background Execution Engine**.

