# 40. Application Delegate Integration

The actual application lifecycle remains the owner of UIKit delegate callbacks.

Conceptually:

```swift
@MainActor
final class ApplicationDelegate:
    NSObject,
    UIApplicationDelegate
{
    private let pushRouter =
        PushEventRouter()

    private lazy var notificationDelegate =
        ApplicationNotificationDelegate(
            router:
                pushRouter
        )

    func application(
        _ application:
            UIApplication,
        didFinishLaunchingWithOptions
            launchOptions:
                [UIApplication.LaunchOptionsKey: Any]? = nil
    ) -> Bool {

        UNUserNotificationCenter.current()
            .delegate =
            notificationDelegate

        Task {
            await PushRuntime.shared.start()
        }

        return true
    }

    func application(
        _ application:
            UIApplication,
        didRegisterForRemoteNotificationsWithDeviceToken
            deviceToken:
                Data
    ) {

        Task {
            await PushRuntime.shared
                .registerToken(
                    deviceToken
                )
        }
    }

    func application(
        _ application:
            UIApplication,
        didFailToRegisterForRemoteNotificationsWithError
            error:
                Error
    ) {

        Logger.push.error(
            """
            APNs registration failed:
            \(error.localizedDescription)
            """
        )
    }
}
```

The exact lifecycle arrangement should follow the application's existing SwiftUI `App` / scene architecture rather than introducing a second `@main`.

---

# 41. Info.plist

Push notification capability requires the appropriate application configuration and APNs entitlement.

The runtime itself cannot grant those capabilities.

For a real application, configure:

```text
Signing & Capabilities
    └── Push Notifications

Background Modes
    ├── Remote notifications
    └── Other modes only when actually required
```

Do not enable background modes simply to obtain additional execution time.

---

# 42. Backend Boundary

The iPhone runtime should not directly contain APNs server credentials.

Correct architecture:

```text
                    iPHONE
                       │
                       │ authenticated HTTPS
                       ▼
                 APPLICATION API
                       │
                       ▼
                 PUSH SERVICE
                       │
                       ▼
                      APNs
                       │
                       ▼
                    iPHONE
```

The APNs provider authentication key belongs on the server.

Never ship:

```text
.p8 APNs private key
APNs provider secret
server signing credentials
CloudKit server credentials
```

inside the iPhone application.

