        │
#9   Sensor & Hardware Abstraction
        │
#10  Master Runtime & Diagnostics
        │
#11  Advanced Memory Manager
        │
#12  GPU / Metal Compute
        │
#13  Advanced Camera & Imaging
        │
#14  Media & Audio
        │
#15  Database / Query Engine
        │
#16  Cloud / iCloud
        │
#17  Push Notification Engine
        │
#18  Background Execution Engine
```

## Responsibility boundaries

```text
#3  decides:
    "Should we spend energy?"

#4  decides:
    "How should network transport happen?"

#15 decides:
    "What is durable local state?"

#16 decides:
    "How does local state synchronize?"

#17 decides:
    "How does the user receive an event?"

#18 decides:
    "When iOS gives us execution time,
     what bounded work should we perform?"

#10 decides:
    "Is the overall runtime healthy?"
```

## Important iOS boundary

This architecture does **not** attempt to:

* keep arbitrary code running indefinitely in the background
* bypass iOS scheduling
* bypass Low Power Mode
* bypass thermal management
* bypass user notification settings
* force background execution
* create a permanent background daemon
* prevent the system from suspending the application

Those decisions remain under iOS control.

The runtime instead makes the application's background work **bounded, cancellable, persistent where necessary, power-aware, and restart-safe**.

---

# 41. Recommended Integration Order

The next production integration should be:

```text
#18 Background
       │
       ├── #3 Power/Thermal
       │
       ├── #4 Networking
       │
       ├── #15 Database
       │
       ├── #16 Cloud
       │
       ├── #17 Push
       │
       └── #10 Master Runtime
```

Then the architecture is ready for the next major platform layer:

**#19 — App Extension Runtime**, covering WidgetKit, App Intents, Share Extensions, Action Extensions, notification extensions, Live Activities, extension-safe shared storage, lifecycle constraints, and the security boundary between the main application and its extensions.



# iPhone App Extension Runtime — Swift

## #19 App Extension Runtime

### Architecture

```text
                         iOS
                          │
        ┌─────────────────┼──────────────────┐
        │                 │                  │
        ▼                 ▼                  ▼
    MAIN APP          EXTENSIONS          SYSTEM UI
        │                 │                  │
        │       ┌─────────┼─────────┐        │
        │       │         │         │        │
        │       ▼         ▼         ▼        │
        │    Widget    AppIntent   Share     │
        │       │         │         │        │
        │       └─────────┼─────────┘        │
        │                 │                  │
        └────────────┬────┴──────────────────┘
                     ▼
             SHARED APP STATE
                     │
          ┌──────────┼──────────┐
          ▼          ▼          ▼
       #15 DB      #7 Security  #6 UI
          │
          ▼
      App Group
```

The extension runtime must remain:

* lightweight
* deterministic
* cancellation-aware
* memory bounded
* independent of the main application process
* safe to terminate at any time
* based entirely on public extension APIs

