                #17              │
                Push              │
                 │                │
                 ▼                ▼
               #18 ─────────► App Group
            Background            │
                                  ▼
                         Widget / Intent /
                         Share / Live Activity
```

The resulting design keeps the **full runtime in the main application**, while #19 exposes carefully controlled, low-memory interfaces to Apple's extension environments. This prevents a Widget, Share Extension, or App Intent from accidentally dragging the entire performance, camera, AI, networking, and cloud stack into a short-lived extension process.






# iPhone Multitasking & Scene Manager — Swift

## #20 Multitasking & Scene Manager

### System architecture

```text
                         iOS
                          │
                 Scene Sessions
                          │
              ┌───────────┼───────────┐
              ▼           ▼           ▼
          Scene A      Scene B      Scene C
              │           │           │
              ▼           ▼           ▼
           UI State    UI State    UI State
              │           │           │
              └──────┬────┴──────┬────┘
                     ▼           ▼
                 #6 UI       #20 Scene Manager
                     │           │
                     └─────┬─────┘
                           ▼
                     #10 Master Runtime
                           │
          ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
          ▼                ▼                ▼
         #3               #18              #19
       Power          Background       Extensions
```

#20 owns **scene lifecycle and prioritisation**.

It does not replace SwiftUI/UIKit scene management and does not attempt to control iOS's private window compositor.

