# 26. Power Integration — #3

Scene state should directly influence application workload.

```text
ACTIVE
  │
  ▼
Full UI workload
  │
  ├── rendering
  ├── networking
  ├── AI
  └── sensor processing

INACTIVE
  │
  ▼
Reduced workload

BACKGROUND
  │
  ▼
#18 Background Engine
  │
  ▼
Only permitted work

SUSPENDED
  │
  ▼
No continuous application workload
```

The scene manager should **request** workload reductions from #1/#3/#6/#8 rather than trying to control hardware resources itself.

---

# 27. Scene Power Policy

```swift
public struct ScenePowerDecision:
    Sendable,
    Codable
{
    public let scene:
        ApplicationSceneID

    public let allowRendering:
        Bool

    public let allowNetworkPrefetch:
        Bool

    public let allowInference:
        Bool

    public let allowSensorUpdates:
        Bool

    public init(
        scene:
            ApplicationSceneID,
        allowRendering:
            Bool,
        allowNetworkPrefetch:
            Bool,
        allowInference:
            Bool,
        allowSensorUpdates:
            Bool
    ) {
        self.scene =
            scene

        self.allowRendering =
            allowRendering

        self.allowNetworkPrefetch =
            allowNetworkPrefetch

        self.allowInference =
            allowInference

        self.allowSensorUpdates =
            allowSensorUpdates
    }
}
```

Example policy:

```text
ACTIVE
rendering       YES
network         YES
AI              YES
sensors         YES

INACTIVE
rendering       REDUCED
network         LIMITED
AI              LIMITED
sensors         LIMITED

BACKGROUND
rendering       NO
network         ONLY WHEN PERMITTED
AI              ONLY WHEN PERMITTED
sensors         ONLY WHEN REQUIRED
```

---

# 28. UI Rendering Integration — #6

#6 receives scene-specific rendering demand.

```swift
