This lets #6 decide how aggressively to invalidate/update views.

---

# 29. Network Integration — #4

A background scene should not automatically inherit foreground network behaviour.

```text
Scene A ACTIVE
     │
     └── high-priority requests

Scene B INACTIVE
     │
     └── ordinary requests

Scene C BACKGROUND
     │
     └── no speculative requests
```

The actual request policy remains owned by #4.

---

# 30. AI Integration — #8

```swift
public enum SceneAIAllowance:
    String,
    Sendable,
    Codable
{
    case unrestricted
    case reduced
    case deferred
    case prohibited
}
```

Scene state can be translated into an AI workload policy:

```text
ACTIVE       → unrestricted
INACTIVE     → reduced
BACKGROUND   → deferred
SUSPENDED    → prohibited
```

This is an application-level policy only.

---

# 31. Camera Integration — #13

Only an active camera scene should normally maintain an interactive preview.

```text
Camera Scene
     │
     ▼
ACTIVE
     │
     ├── preview
     ├── frame processing
     └── UI rendering

Scene becomes background
     │
     ▼
#13 evaluates capture policy
     │
     ▼
stop / reduce / transition
```

Whether capture may continue depends on the application's legitimate iOS background/capture configuration.

The scene manager does not bypass iOS background restrictions.

---

# 32. Audio Integration — #14

Audio is different because legitimate audio applications can have background behaviour.

Therefore:

```text
Scene inactive
     │
     ├── ordinary app → reduce/stop
     │
     └── active audio session → #14 decides
```

#20 should send lifecycle information to #14 but should not blindly shut down an audio engine.

---

# 33. Extension Integration — #19

Extensions have their own process and lifecycle.

```text
Main Scene
    │
    ▼
#20 Scene Manager
    │
    ▼
#19 Extension Runtime
    │
    ├── Widget
    ├── App Intent
    ├── Share
    └── Live Activity
```

An extension should never be assumed to share the main application's scene lifecycle.

---

# 34. External Display

External-display scenes can use a dedicated role:

```swift
let descriptor =
    SceneDescriptor(
        id:
            ApplicationSceneID(
                value:
                    "external-display"
            ),
        role:
