# 20. Peer Runtime Boundary

The actual `MCSession`, `MCNearbyServiceBrowser`, and delegate objects should remain inside a dedicated platform adapter because those framework objects have UIKit/Foundation reference semantics and are not useful application-state models.

```swift
@MainActor
public protocol PeerConnectivityAdapter:
    AnyObject
{
    func start()
    func stop()

    func invite(
        peer:
            PeerDescriptor
    )

    func send(
        data:
            Data,
        to:
            PeerDescriptor
    ) throws
}
```

A concrete `MultipeerConnectivity` adapter can then implement this protocol inside the application target.

