# 41. Security Boundary

Connectivity does not own credentials.

```text
#21
 │
 └── endpoint/route discovery

#4
 │
 └── HTTP/network transport

#7
 │
 └── credentials/tokens/keys
```

Never put:

```text
passwords
private keys
access tokens
session secrets
```

into Bonjour service metadata, peer discovery payloads, logs or connectivity telemetry.

---

# 42. Performance Rules

The runtime should obey these rules:

```text
DO

✓ observe NWPathMonitor
✓ use async/await
✓ bound connection counts
✓ reuse connections
✓ cancel unused connections
✓ avoid polling
✓ defer expensive work on expensive paths
✓ keep discovery scoped
✓ use OSLog diagnostics
✓ persist important telemetry through #15

DON'T

✗ poll network state every few milliseconds
✗ create a new connection for every packet
✗ continuously scan the local network
✗ keep unnecessary peer sessions alive
✗ send secrets through discovery
✗ assume Wi-Fi means Internet access
✗ assume cellular is unlimited
✗ assume background execution is guaranteed
```

