## Core principle

**#4 manages network requests.**

**#21 manages connectivity intelligence.**

That separation prevents the application from accumulating multiple competing networking stacks.

The resulting iPhone platform now has:

```text
#1  Performance
#2  Memory
#3  Power/Thermal
#4  Networking
#5  Storage
#6  Rendering
#7  Security
#8  Intelligence
#9  Hardware
#10 Master Runtime

#11 Advanced Memory
#12 Metal/GPU
#13 Camera/Imaging
#14 Audio/Media
#15 Database
#16 Cloud/iCloud
#17 Push
#18 Background
#19 Extensions
#20 Multitasking/Scenes
#21 Advanced Connectivity
```

This gives the stack a proper **connectivity intelligence layer** rather than simply treating networking as `URLSession` calls.






# iPhone Device Attestation & Application Integrity Runtime — Swift

## #22 Device Attestation & Application Integrity Runtime

### Architecture

```text
                         iOS
                          │
          ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐
          ▼               ▼                ▼
      App Attest       DeviceCheck      Secure Enclave
          │               │                │
          └───────────────┼────────────────┘
                          ▼
               #22 ATTESTATION RUNTIME
                          │
          ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐
          ▼               ▼                ▼
      Key lifecycle    Challenges       Assertions
          │               │                │
          └───────────────┼────────────────┘
                          ▼
                    #7 Security
                          │
                          ▼
                    #4 Networking
                          │
                          ▼
                 Backend Verification
                          │
                          ▼
                    #10 Master Runtime
```

The central rule is:

```text
iPhone app
    │
    │ attestation/assertion
    ▼
backend
    │
    ├── verifies cryptographically
    ├── validates challenge
    ├── checks app identity
    └── applies server-side policy
```

**The client does not decide that its own attestation is valid.**

---

