# 47. Important Platform Boundary

This runtime deliberately does **not** attempt to provide:

```text
private Secure Enclave commands
private kernel integrity APIs
jailbreak detection based on private APIs
private process inspection
private filesystem inspection
private code-signing interfaces
private Apple server protocols
hardware-level anti-tamper controls
```

Those are outside the public iOS application API model.

Instead, the architecture uses:

```text
App Attest
DeviceCheck
Keychain
Secure Enclave
CryptoKit
LocalAuthentication
HTTPS
server-side verification
```

---

# 48. Complete Security Architecture

```text
                        #22
                DEVICE ATTESTATION
                         │
          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
          ▼              ▼              ▼
     App Attest      DeviceCheck    Challenge
          │              │              │
          └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                         ▼
                       #7
                 SECURITY RUNTIME
                         │
          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
          ▼              ▼              ▼
       Keychain     Secure Enclave   CryptoKit
          │              │              │
          └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                         ▼
                       #4
                    NETWORKING
                         │
                         ▼
                      HTTPS
                         │
                         ▼
                     BACKEND
                         │
                cryptographic proof
                         │
                         ▼
                  authorization
```

---

# 49. iPhone Runtime Stack — #1–#22

```text
#1   Performance Runtime
#2   Memory Management
#3   Battery & Thermal
#4   Networking & Connectivity
#5   Persistent Storage
#6   UI & Rendering
#7   Security & Privacy
#8   On-device Intelligence
#9   Sensor & Hardware
#10  Master Runtime & Diagnostics

#11  Advanced Memory Manager
#12  GPU / Metal Compute
#13  Advanced Camera & Imaging
#14  Media & Audio Engine
#15  Database / Query Engine
#16  Cloud / iCloud Runtime
#17  Push Notification Engine
#18  Background Execution Runtime
#19  App Extension Runtime
#20  Multitasking & Scene Manager
#21  Advanced Connectivity
#22  Device Attestation & Application Integrity
```

### Final #22 responsibility

```text
                  TRUST BOUNDARY

        ┌─────────────────────────────┐
        │         iPhone App          │
        │                             │
        │ #7 Cryptography & Secrets   │
        │ #22 Attestation             │
        └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                       │
                  cryptographic
                     evidence
                       │
                       ▼
        ┌─────────────────────────────┐
        │          Backend            │
        │                             │
        │ Verify → Authenticate →     │
        │ Authorize → Execute         │
        └─────────────────────────────┘
```

**#22 therefore establishes an application-integrity/attestation layer without pretending that the iPhone can verify itself.** The cryptographic decision ultimately belongs to the backend, while #7 remains responsible for the application's secrets and cryptographic primitives.






# iPhone #23 — Advanced AI Runtime

## 1. Purpose

#8 provides the foundational **on-device intelligence execution layer**.

#23 becomes the higher-level **AI orchestration layer**:

```text
                    APPLICATION
                         │
                         ▼
                #23 ADVANCED AI
                    RUNTIME
                         │
        ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
        │                │                │
        ▼                ▼                ▼
   Foundation        Core ML /       Vision / Speech
     Models          Core AI           / Media
        │                │                │
        └────────────────┼────────────────┘
                         ▼
                  AI GOVERNOR
                         │
             ┌───────────┼───────────┐
             ▼           ▼           ▼
           LOCAL      DEFER       CLOUD/PCC
                         │
                         ▼
                  #3 Power/Thermal
                  #11 Memory
                  #12 Metal
                  #4 Network
                  #7 Security
                  #10 Master Runtime
```

The runtime therefore answers:

```text
What model?
Where should it run?
How much memory?
How much context?
What tools can it call?
Can it run now?
Should it remain local?
Should it use a server?
What happens if the model is unavailable?
```

---

# 2. Framework Boundaries

For modern Apple platforms, the runtime can use:

```swift
import Foundation
import CoreML
import Vision
import OSLog
import Observation
```

Foundation Models should be conditionally compiled where the deployment target supports it:

```swift
#if canImport(FoundationModels)
import FoundationModels
#endif
```

Apple's Foundation Models framework provides `LanguageModelSession`, structured generation, tool calling and multimodal capabilities.

