```

## #23 operating principles

```text
1. Local-first when practical.
2. Never expose the entire application database to a model.
3. Use structured generation instead of fragile text parsing.
4. Treat tools as explicitly permissioned capabilities.
5. Keep destructive actions behind application authorization.
6. Bound context size.
7. Bound memory.
8. Bound inference concurrency.
9. Integrate with #3 power and thermal policy.
10. Integrate with #11 memory management.
11. Integrate with #12 GPU/Metal.
12. Integrate with #13 imaging.
13. Integrate with #14 audio.
14. Integrate with #15 database.
15. Integrate with #16 cloud.
16. Integrate with #17 push.
17. Integrate with #18 background execution.
18. Integrate with #19 extensions.
19. Integrate with #20 scenes.
20. Integrate with #22 attestation for protected server actions.
21. Version prompts and AI behavior.
22. Evaluate AI behavior before production deployment.
23. Never claim control over Apple's private AI hardware infrastructure.
```

### Result

#23 turns the existing stack from a collection of ML capabilities into an **application-level AI operating layer**:

```text
              USER / APP
                  │
                  ▼
          ┌───────────────┐
          │ #23 AI RUNTIME│
          └───────┬───────┘
                  │
        ┌─────────┼──────────┐
        ▼         ▼          ▼
     UNDERSTAND  REASON     ACT
        │         │          │
        ▼         ▼          ▼
      Vision   Foundation   Tools
      Speech     Models      │
      Core ML       │        │
        │           │        │
        └───────────┼────────┘
                    ▼
              POLICY ENGINE
                    │
       ┌────────────┼─────────────┐
       ▼            ▼             ▼
     LOCAL       DEFER         CLOUD/PCC
       │            │             │
       └────────────┼─────────────┘
                    ▼
            RESULT / ACTION
```

That gives the iPhone stack a modern **AI orchestration layer** rather than simply adding another model wrapper. Apple currently positions Foundation Models, Core AI, Vision, Core ML and evaluation tooling as complementary pieces of its on-device AI ecosystem, which maps naturally onto this layered architecture.






# iPhone #24 — Maps & Geospatial Runtime

## 1. Purpose

The #24 runtime provides the application's geographic intelligence layer:

```text
                         APPLICATION
                              │
                              ▼
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │ #24 GEO RUNTIME   │
                    └────────┬─────────┘
                             │
       ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
       ▼                     ▼                     ▼
 Core Location           MapKit               Geocoding
       │                     │                     │
       ▼                     ▼                     ▼
 GPS / location        maps / routes          addresses
       │                     │                     │
       └─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┘
                             ▼
                    GEOSPATIAL ENGINE
                             │
              ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
              ▼              ▼              ▼
          Geofencing      Search         Spatial AI
              │              │              │
              ▼              ▼              ▼
             #15            #4             #23
          Database       Network            AI
```

The runtime is responsible for:

* location acquisition
* authorization
* location quality
* geographic coordinates
* distance calculations
* bearings
* routes
* map-region state
* geocoding
* reverse geocoding
* geofencing
* spatial indexing
* place/search integration
* location history
* power-aware tracking
* AI geographic context
* scene-specific map state
* diagnostics

It does **not** attempt to access private GPS/baseband functionality.

