# 58. Production Rules

```text
1. Core Location stays behind a controlled boundary.
2. CLLocation objects should not leak through the whole architecture.
3. Use Sendable geographic value types.
4. Location history is opt-in.
5. Don't write every location sample to disk.
6. Don't upload every location sample to iCloud.
7. Don't send precise location to AI unnecessarily.
8. Use geofencing for event-driven geographic behaviour.
9. Use MapKit for maps/search/routing rather than reinventing them.
10. Use #4 for application networking.
11. Use #15 for durable storage.
12. Use #16 for synchronization.
13. Use #3 for power-aware tracking policy.
14. Use #6 for rendering.
15. Use #20 for scene-specific map state.
16. Use #23 for controlled spatial AI.
17. Keep Core Location/MapKit objects on appropriate platform isolation boundaries.
18. Cancel route/search work when no longer required.
19. Bound spatial queries.
20. Never claim access to private GPS, baseband, Apple Maps servers, or navigation internals.
```

