# 29. #15 Database Integration

The database remains authoritative:

```text
                 #15 DATABASE
                       │
          ┌────────────┴────────────┐
          ▼                         ▼
       records                   changes
          │                         │
          └────────────┬────────────┘
                       ▼
                  #25 INDEXER
                       │
                       ▼
                  SEARCH INDEX
```

For example:

```swift
let document =
    SearchDocument(
        id:
            "document-123",
        domain:
            .documents,
        title:
            "Yorkshire Infrastructure Report",
        body:
            "Regional rail and energy infrastructure...",
        keywords:
            [
                "Yorkshire",
                "rail",
                "energy"
            ],
        createdAt:
            Date(),
        modifiedAt:
            Date()
    )

await SearchRuntime
    .shared
    .index(
        document:
            document
    )
```

Then:

```swift
let results =
    await SearchRuntime
        .shared
        .search(
            SearchQuery(
                text:
                    "Yorkshire rail"
            )
        )
```

---

# 30. #16 Cloud Integration

Cloud synchronization should update #15.

```text
#16 CLOUD
   │
   ▼
#15 DATABASE
   │
   ▼
change detected
   │
   ▼
#25 INDEXER
   │
   ▼
local search
```

The cloud should **not** become the search index.

This keeps search functional when offline.

---

# 31. #24 Geospatial Integration

A result can contain coordinates without making the text index responsible for geographic calculations.

```text
#25 SEARCH
    │
    ▼
candidate documents
    │
    ▼
#24 GEO
    │
    ├── distance
    ├── bounding box
    └── nearest point
```

Example application query:

```text
"restaurant"
within 5 km
```

The textual search happens first; #24 then performs geographic filtering.

---

# 32. #23 AI Integration

AI should be an **optional second-stage ranker**, not the first thing invoked for every keystroke.

```text
User Query
    │
    ▼
#25 lexical search
    │
    ▼
top 50 candidates
    │
    ▼
#23 semantic ranking
    │
    ▼
top 10
    │
    ▼
UI
```

This reduces unnecessary inference.

A future interface:

```swift
public protocol SemanticSearchRanker:
    Sendable
{
    func rerank(
        query:
            String,
        results:
            [SearchResult]
    )
        async
        -> [SearchResult]
}
```

#23 can then provide a Core ML implementation without making #25 dependent on a specific AI model.

---

# 33. Search Ranking Pipeline

```text
                         QUERY
                           │
                           ▼
                       tokenize
                           │
                           ▼
                       normalize
                           │
                           ▼
                     inverted index
                           │
                           ▼
                       candidates
                           │
                           ▼
                       lexical rank
                           │
                    ┌──────┴──────┐
                    ▼             ▼
                 filters       #24 geo
                    │             │
                    └──────┬──────┘
                           ▼
                     optional #23
                       reranking
                           │
                           ▼
                         LIMIT
                           │
                           ▼
                          UI
```

---

# 34. #19 Extension Integration

Extensions should use compact search APIs.

```text
Widget
  │
  ▼
#19 Extension
  │
  ▼
small search request
  │
  ▼
#25
  │
  ▼
compact results
```

Do not instantiate the entire search index inside every extension target.

