---

# 48. Full #25 Architecture

```text
                         ┌─────────────────┐
                         │ #10 MASTER      │
                         └────────┬────────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
                         ┌─────────────────┐
                         │ #25 SEARCH      │
                         └────────┬────────┘
                                  │
               ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐
               │                  │                  │
               ▼                  ▼                  ▼
          TOKENIZER          INDEXER             CACHE
               │                  │                  │
               │                  ▼                  │
               │             #15 DATABASE            │
               │                  │                  │
               └──────────┬───────┴──────────────────┘
                          ▼
                    SEARCH ENGINE
                          │
                 ┌────────┼─────────┐
                 ▼        ▼         ▼
              FILTER     #24       #23
                         GEO        AI
                 │        │         │
                 └────────┼─────────┘
                          ▼
                       RESULTS
                          │
                          ▼
                         #6 UI
```

---

# 49. Final Design Principle

The most important rule for #25 is:

```text
DATABASE ≠ SEARCH INDEX
SEARCH INDEX ≠ AI
AI ≠ DATABASE
```

Instead:

```text
                #15
             authoritative
                state
                  │
                  ▼
                #25
          deterministic search
                  │
          ┌───────┴────────┐
          ▼                ▼
         #24              #23
       spatial          semantic
       context           ranking
          │                │
          └───────┬────────┘
                  ▼
                 UI
```

That gives the iPhone runtime a search architecture that is **fast locally, offline-capable, rebuildable, memory-bounded, privacy-conscious, and extensible to semantic AI without making every search query an AI workload.**






# iPhone #26 — Document & File System Runtime — Swift

## 1. Purpose

#26 provides a unified application-level document and file runtime.

```text
                         #10 MASTER RUNTIME
                                │
                                ▼
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │ #26 DOCUMENT / FILE  │
                    │       RUNTIME         │
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │
        ┌──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┐
        ▼                      ▼                      ▼
    LOCAL FILES             #15 DATA               #16 CLOUD
    DOCUMENTS               ENGINE                 iCLOUD
        │                      │                      │
        └──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┘
                               ▼
                           #25 SEARCH
                               │
                               ▼
                              #6 UI
```

Responsibilities:

* application documents
* file import/export
* document metadata
* atomic writes
* file versioning
* security-scoped resources
* document-provider integration boundary
* file coordination boundary
* iCloud document containers
* previews
* MIME/UTType classification
* bounded file access
* checksums
* duplicate detection
* file indexing
* document lifecycle
* storage metrics
* diagnostics
* integration with #15, #16, #19 and #25

The runtime **does not replace the iOS filesystem** and does not claim unrestricted access to the device filesystem.

---

# 2. Imports

```swift
import Foundation
import UniformTypeIdentifiers
import OSLog
import Observation
import SwiftUI
```

UIKit-dependent document picker integration is kept behind a separate MainActor boundary later in this file.

---

# 3. File Domains

```swift
public enum FileDomain:
    String,
    Codable,
    Sendable
{
    case applicationDocuments
    case applicationSupport
    case caches
    case temporary
    case imported
    case exported
    case sharedContainer
    case iCloudDocuments
}
```

---

# 4. File Identifier

Paths should not be used as the primary application identity.

