# 22. Security-Scoped Resource

Files selected through document-provider APIs can require security-scoped access.

```swift
public actor SecurityScopedResourceManager {

    private var active:
        Set<String> = []

    public init() {}

    public func start(
        _ url:
            URL
    )
        throws
    {
        guard
            url.startAccessingSecurityScopedResource()
        else {
            throw FileRuntimeError
                .securityScopeRequired
        }

        active.insert(
            url.absoluteString
        )
    }

    public func stop(
        _ url:
            URL
    ) {

        let key =
            url.absoluteString

        guard
            active.contains(
                key
            )
        else {
            return
        }

        url.stopAccessingSecurityScopedResource()

        active.remove(
            key
        )
    }
}
```

The application must balance every successful access with a corresponding stop.

