# 42. Startup

#10 should initialise #26 after #15:

```text
#10 MASTER
    │
    ├── #15 Database
    │       │
    │       ▼
    │     #26 Files
    │       │
    │       ▼
    │     #25 Search
    │
    └── #16 Cloud
```

This gives the storage hierarchy:

```text
                    #15 DATABASE
                         │
          ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
          ▼                             ▼
    structured data                file metadata
                                        │
                                        ▼
                                   #26 FILES
                                        │
                         ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
                         ▼              ▼              ▼
                      local         iCloud        App Groups
                         │              │              │
                         └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                                        ▼
                                     #25 SEARCH
```

---

# 43. Power Integration

Large file operations should cooperate with #3.

```text
#3 POWER / THERMAL
        │
        ▼
#26 FILE POLICY
        │
        ├── foreground → normal I/O
        ├── low power  → defer indexing
        └── thermal    → defer previews
```

The runtime should not perform expensive document extraction or indexing merely because a file changed.

---

# 44. Memory Integration

#11 should control large buffers.

```text
File
 │
 ▼
#26
 │
 ├── small → Data
 │
 └── large → streaming
                │
                ▼
              #11
           memory budget
```

A production implementation should avoid:

```text
4 GB file
   ↓
Data(contentsOf:)
   ↓
4 GB allocation
```

and instead use bounded streaming.

---

# 45. Security Integration

#7 protects secrets and credentials.

#26 manages documents.

Therefore:

```text
#7 SECURITY
    │
    ├── credentials
    ├── keys
    ├── authentication
    └── protected secrets

#26 DOCUMENTS
    │
    ├── user documents
    ├── imports
    ├── exports
    └── application files
```

Do not place Keychain/Secure Enclave material into ordinary document files unless there is a deliberate cryptographic design.

---

# 46. Cloud Integration

```text
LOCAL FILE
    │
    ▼
#26
    │
    ▼
#16 CLOUD
    │
    ▼
iCloud / CloudKit
```

The synchronization policy determines what actually leaves the device.

Not every local file should automatically become cloud data.

---

# 47. Extension Integration

#19 extensions can access explicitly shared data through App Groups.

```text
MAIN APP
   │
   ▼
#26
   │
   ▼
APP GROUP
   │
   ├── Widget
   ├── Share Extension
   ├── App Intent
   └── Other supported extensions
```

Extensions should use compact files/state rather than opening the entire application's document database.

