Again, this controls whether the **application submits optional work**. It does not control Metal hardware clocks.

---

# 28. Network Integration

Networking can be treated differently from CPU/GPU work.

A network transfer may be:

```text
large upload
    │
    ▼
#27 budget check
    │
    ▼
#28 thermal forecast
    │
    ├── normal → continue
    ├── elevated → reduce ancillary work
    └── severe → defer optional transfer
```

This should be coordinated with #4's network conditions rather than making thermal state the only decision variable.

---

# 29. File/Search Integration

#26 and #25 are ideal candidates for thermal-aware deferral.

```text
DOCUMENT CHANGES
       │
       ▼
     #26
       │
       ▼
INDEX REQUEST
       │
       ▼
     #28
       │
       ├── LOW → index
       ├── ELEVATED → batch
       ├── HIGH → defer
       └── SEVERE → pause
```

This prevents background indexing from competing with foreground camera, audio, graphics or AI workloads.

