#25 Search / Indexing
#26 Document / File System
#27 Energy Budget / Resource Accounting
#28 Thermal Prediction / Forecasting
```

The architecture now has a proper **closed-loop resource-control layer**:

```text
                 OBSERVE
                    │
                    ▼
              ┌───────────┐
              │ #27 USAGE │
              └─────┬─────┘
                    │
                    ▼
              ┌───────────┐
              │ #28 MODEL │
              └─────┬─────┘
                    │
                    ▼
             PREDICT PRESSURE
                    │
                    ▼
              ┌───────────┐
              │   #27     │
              │  GOVERNOR │
              └─────┬─────┘
                    │
          ┌─────────┼─────────┐
          ▼         ▼         ▼
        RUN      THROTTLE   DEFER
          │         │         │
          └─────────┼─────────┘
                    ▼
                 OBSERVE
```

**#29 should therefore be Automated Diagnostics & Runtime Verification**: a test/health layer capable of continuously checking #1–#28 for faults, latency regressions, resource leaks, actor stalls, failed dependencies, degraded subsystems, corrupted persisted state, networking failures, and thermal/power policy violations.




# iPhone #29 — Automated Diagnostics & Runtime Verification — Swift

## 1. Role in the architecture

#29 sits alongside the master runtime and observes every major subsystem.

```text
                         #10 MASTER RUNTIME
                                │
                                ▼
                    ┌───────────────────────┐
                    │ #29 DIAGNOSTICS       │
                    │ & RUNTIME VERIFICATION│
                    └───────────┬───────────┘
                                │
       ┌────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┐
       ▼                        ▼                        ▼
   HEALTH CHECKS          PERFORMANCE TESTS       INTEGRITY CHECKS
       │                        │                        │
       ▼                        ▼                        ▼
   #01–#28                 #01–#28                 #05/#07/#15/#16/#26
       │                        │                        │
       └────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┘
                                ▼
                       DIAGNOSTIC DECISION
                                │
             ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┐
             ▼                  ▼                  ▼
          HEALTHY           DEGRADED             FAULT
             │                  │                  │
             └──────────────────┼──────────────────┘
                                ▼
                         #10 MASTER RUNTIME
```

The goal is **runtime verification**, not merely logging.

It detects things such as:

* stalled actors
* unexpectedly slow operations
* excessive queue depth
* repeated failures
* failed subsystem startup
* memory/cache growth
* thermal policy violations
* networking degradation
* persistence failures
* cloud synchronization problems
* invalid runtime state
* excessive cancellation
* watchdog timeouts
* unexpected workload duration
* diagnostic regressions

