# 37. Automated Regression Detection

#29 can compare current measurements against a baseline.

```swift
public struct DiagnosticBaseline:
    Codable,
    Sendable
{
    public let operation:
        String

    public let expectedMilliseconds:
        Double

    public let allowedMultiplier:
        Double

    public init(
        operation:
            String,
        expectedMilliseconds:
            Double,
        allowedMultiplier:
            Double = 1.5
    ) {
        self.operation =
            operation

        self.expectedMilliseconds =
            expectedMilliseconds

        self.allowedMultiplier =
            max(
                1,
                allowedMultiplier
            )
    }

    public func accepts(
        milliseconds:
            Double
    )
        -> Bool
    {
        milliseconds <=
            expectedMilliseconds *
            allowedMultiplier
    }
}
```

This enables:

```text
build A
  image decode = 18 ms

build B
  image decode = 22 ms

baseline = 18 ms
allowed = 27 ms

→ within baseline
```

versus:

```text
build C
  image decode = 51 ms

→ regression detected
```

---

# 38. Actor Stall Detection

Actors should periodically heartbeat:

```swift
let watchdog =
    await AutomatedDiagnosticsRuntime
        .shared
        .engine
        .getWatchdog()

let id =
    await watchdog.register(
        name:
            "DatabaseRuntime",
        timeout:
            5
    )

await watchdog.heartbeat(
    id:
        id
)
```

A production subsystem should heartbeat at meaningful progress points rather than every trivial operation.

