#29 therefore becomes the **runtime nervous system for reliability**: #1–#28 perform the work, while #29 continuously asks whether that work is still behaving within the application's declared performance, resource, thermal, persistence, security and lifecycle contracts.




# iPhone #30 — Developer Instrumentation & Performance Telemetry — Swift

## 1. Architecture

```text
                         iPHONE RUNTIME
                              │
                    ┌─────────┴─────────┐
                    │                   │
                 #10 MASTER          #29
                 RUNTIME          DIAGNOSTICS
                    │                   │
                    └─────────┬─────────┘
                              ▼
                    ┌───────────────────┐
                    │ #30 INSTRUMENTATION│
                    │ & TELEMETRY       │
                    └─────────┬─────────┘
                              │
       ┌──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┐
       ▼                      ▼                      ▼
   SIGNPOSTS              METRICS                TRACES
       │                      │                      │
       ▼                      ▼                      ▼
   OSLog /                counters              spans
   Instruments            histograms             events
                              │
                              ▼
                    PERFORMANCE TIMELINE
                              │
             ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
             ▼                ▼                ▼
          CPU/GPU          MEMORY           NETWORK
             │                │                │
             └────────────────┼────────────────┘
                              ▼
