# 44. Performance Budget Verification

#30 can feed latency results directly into #29.

```swift
public struct PerformanceBudgetVerifier:
    Sendable
{
    public init() {}

    public func verify(
        operation:
            String,
        histogram:
            LatencyHistogram,
        p95Budget:
            Double
    )
        -> Bool
    {
        histogram.percentile(
            0.95
        ) <= p95Budget
    }
}
```

The intended relationship is:

```text
#30 measures
       │
       ▼
histogram
       │
       ▼
p95 / p99
       │
       ▼
#29 verifies
       │
       ▼
finding if regression
```

---

# 45. Production/Development Separation

The runtime should make it difficult to accidentally ship expensive tracing.

```swift
#if DEBUG

let configuration =
    InstrumentationConfiguration
        .development

#else

let configuration =
    InstrumentationConfiguration
        .release

#endif
```

For profiling builds:

```swift
let configuration =
    InstrumentationConfiguration
        .profiling
```

---

# 46. Signpost Strategy

Use instrumentation at **system boundaries**, not everywhere.

Recommended:

```text
GOOD
────────────────────────────
camera.capture
camera.process
ai.inference
database.transaction
cloud.sync
network.request
document.import
document.export
render.pass
background.task
scene.transition

AVOID
────────────────────────────
every property getter
every array access
every actor message
every SwiftUI body evaluation
every pixel
every sensor sample
```

Instrumentation should remain cheaper than the operation being measured whenever practical.

---

# 47. Complete Observability Stack

The iPhone architecture now has four distinct layers:

```text
#27
RESOURCE ACCOUNTING
       │
       │
       ▼
#28
THERMAL FORECASTING
       │
       │
       ▼
#29
AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS
       │
       │
       ▼
#30
PERFORMANCE TELEMETRY
```

Their responsibilities are intentionally different.

```text
#27 asks:
"Can we afford this workload?"

#28 asks:
"What is likely to happen if sustained?"

#29 asks:
"Is the runtime behaving correctly?"

#30 asks:
"Exactly where did the time/resources go?"
```

